DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The nneeaarrbbyyiinntt(), nneeaarrbbyyiinnttff(), and nneeaarrbbyyiinnttll() functions  round  their
       argument  to  an integer value in floating‐point format, using the cur‐
       rent rounding direction (see ffeesseettrroouunndd(3)) and without raising the _i_n_‐
       _e_x_a_c_t exception.  When the current rounding direction  is  to  nearest,
       these  functions  round halfway cases to the even integer in accordance
       with IEEE‐754.

       The rriinntt(), rriinnttff(), and rriinnttll() functions do the same, but will  raise
       the  _i_n_e_x_a_c_t exception (FFEE__IINNEEXXAACCTT, checkable via ffeetteesstteexxcceepptt(3)) when
       the result differs in value from the argument.

